{title: Through Him Who Gives Me Strength}
{subtitle: Philippians 4:13}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Cm7] |
| [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]He wrote a word of thanks to friends who'd [Bb]sent him help again
He was [Cm7]writing from a prison, he was [Ab]sitting there in chains
He had [Eb]known the crowded table and he'd [Bb]known the empty bowl
But what[Cm7]ever came, a quiet strength was [Ab]rooted in his soul
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Bb]I have learned to be [Cm]content whatever my cir[Ab]cumstances
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I can do [Eb]all things [Bb]through him who gives [Cm7]me [Ab]strength
I can do [Eb]all things
Through [Bb]him who gives me [Eb]strength
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When the paycheck's gone too [Bb]early and the rent is due again
[Cm7]When the doctor's words are heavy [Ab]and I cannot see the end
[Eb]When the house is full of [Bb]laughter and the cupboards overflow
[Cm7]In every single season he's [Ab]the only strength I [Bb]know
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
I have learned to be [Cm7]content whatever my cir[Ab]cumstances
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I can do all [Eb]things [Bb]through him who gives [Cm7]me [Ab]strength
I can do [Eb]all things
Through [Bb]him who gives me [Cm7]strength [Ab]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]I know what it is to have lit[Cm7]tle
And I know what it is to have plenty
[Ab]Whether well fed or hungry
Whether living in abundance or [Absus2]in want
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I can [Eb]do all things [Bb]through him who gives [Cm7]me [Ab]strength
I can do [Eb]all things
Through [Bb]him who gives me [Cm7]strength [Ab][Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Through [Bb]him who gives me [Cm7]strength [Ab]
{end_of_verse}
